{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791801847,"nonce":"6l0qpNAh+zjj7OOHBr+bEWgIeh8=","message":"Implemented in b9eff9cc1321aafe9a9f22d178c0e11a7098c59d. The bridge now always calls pump_external after the pending-JS callback guard; that function consumes WORK_PENDING and immediately returns for queued work, so no extra sleep or polling timer is introduced. The regression calls native Window.wake immediately after opening the first native-idle window.\n\nmacOS/Metal, Node 24.2.0: the regression failed before the patch with the unchanged 15-second watchdog and the ordinary production addon. After the patch, six fresh production-addon runs pass, including zero idle polls/frames, worker wake around 127ms, loopback I/O, redraw, two simultaneous windows, resize, and pump recreation. native-host, native-scene-window, native-window, native-motion-window and native-hmr individually pass. The isolated acquisition/AppKit/pump trace now reaches a presented first frame by the 713ms sample, with 51 pump calls and two JS notifications, zero surface misses; presentation is asserted before the diagnostic direct wait. Previously there were 351237 notifications and zero pump calls after five seconds.\n\nTypecheck, ESLint and Prettier pass; 62 portable tests pass with loopback networking allowed. Rust clippy --lib --no-deps -- -D warnings passes and rustfmt for the changed bridge file passes. Whole-crate cargo fmt --check reports an existing unformatted set_grid_rows expression in native/src/layout.rs:181 from the prior milestone; this commit leaves it untouched. Generated bindings match after reformatting generated output.\n\nThe full native suite reached motion-window then reproduced the existing spontaneous first-frame failure (60004ms, frames=0, 124 surface misses, no occlusion event); this disproves a claim that the pending-wake patch fixes every 748f2d7 stall. The immediate instrumented motion-window rerun passes. A further 24 instrumented ordinary window runs had no sampled first-frame stall; 23 pass and one native-idle exits on its generic watchdog without a first-frame sample. Added diagnostic-only stage snapshots for future idle watchdogs. Full Linux X11/Wayland CI still required; the approved NUC has no Xvfb/openbox/sway/weston commands installed.\n\nEvidence retained under /private/tmp/blinc-first-frame-startup: native-idle-regression-before.log, wake-reproducer-before-summary.jsonl, wake-reproducer-after.log, fixed-regressions/, native-suite-fixed.log, native-motion-fixed-instrumented.log, fixed-stall-traces/, portable-check-fixed.log, portable-tests-fixed.log. No xwindow/xgpu/ABI production source or dependency pins changed.","files":null}]}